{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"EventMacros","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"EventMacros","modules":[{"name":"EventMacros"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Defining an event","identifiers":["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)"],"anchor":"Defining-an-event"},{"title":"Constraining properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)"],"anchor":"Constraining-properties"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a struct an event. It adds the "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance, the event’s name, consent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"category and schema version when you give them, a "},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" describing each stored property in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration order, and "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances that write each stored property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under its name. "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares rules a plain "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", number or array can’t carry, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a minimum length or a pattern; the macro checks each keyword as it expands, and a tracker rejects an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event whose property breaks one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" includes this module. It re-exports ","type":"text"},{"code":"Events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a file that imports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone can expand the macro too. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol’s documentation, in that module,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shows the conformance written by hand; any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance, Swift’s synthesized one included,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is one a store can write. To export the schemas as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a JSON Schema tracking plan, pass them to ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlans","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    var resultCount: Int","    var filter: String?","}","","let names = SearchPerformed.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"query\", \"resultCount\", \"filter\"]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version:"},{"type":"text","text":" only for a change that records stored at the earlier version can’t be read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through; a store drops those records rather than reading them as the new shape."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers both